WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.946 --> 00:00:19.955
At one o'clock, the servant returned to wake Tom from his nap.

2
00:00:21.696 --> 00:00:24.938
"Is there an outfit that Your Highness prefers to wear this afternoon?"

3
00:00:25.378 --> 00:00:26.298
the servant asked.

4
00:00:26.318 --> 00:00:29.280
"Or shall I choose something for you?"

5
00:00:31.352 --> 00:00:34.034
"I'll just wear the same clothes I had on this morning."

6
00:00:35.876 --> 00:00:36.897
Tom got out of bed.

7
00:00:36.917 --> 00:00:41.821
"I usually wear the same thing all day, every day."

8
00:00:44.223 --> 00:00:47.987
The servant tried to hide his surprise, but he shuffled his feet nervously.

9
00:00:48.007 --> 00:00:54.092
"Begging your pardon, sir, but you always change your clothes before lunch."

10
00:00:56.314 --> 00:00:57.115
Tom laughed.

11
00:00:58.828 --> 00:01:02.131
"And I suppose I'll change into a third outfit before dinner?"

12
00:01:02.151 --> 00:01:04.933
"Of course!"

13
00:01:06.054 --> 00:01:09.177
The servant relaxed, not realizing that Tom was joking.

14
00:01:09.197 --> 00:01:16.663
"You always change before dinner, especially for important events, such as the mayor's banquet this evening."

15
00:01:18.585 --> 00:01:22.709
Tom had never owned new clothes, never mind more than one outfit.

16
00:01:25.591 --> 00:01:28.645
With the servant's help, he was soon dressed for the afternoon.

17
00:01:33.347 --> 00:01:37.629
He was then led into a large room, where some of the furniture was made of gold.

18
00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:42.231
In the center was a table set for one person.

19
00:01:43.852 --> 00:01:47.313
The heavy tablecloth was covered with food in silver dishes.

20
00:01:50.075 --> 00:01:52.296
Tom sat down, eager to begin eating.

21
00:01:54.088 --> 00:01:58.771
But as he reached for a roll, a servant swooped in and tied a napkin around his neck.

22
00:02:00.592 --> 00:02:01.172
"Oh, hello!"

23
00:02:01.612 --> 00:02:02.793
Tom said in surprise.

24
00:02:02.813 --> 00:02:04.454
"Who are you?"

25
00:02:04.474 --> 00:02:10.617
"I'm the royal napkin holder, Your Highness," the man replied.

26
00:02:13.038 --> 00:02:15.400
Tom inspected the napkin covering his clothes.

27
00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:19.602
It was made of snowy white fabric with lace edges.

28
00:02:19.622 --> 00:02:22.924
"This is a beautiful napkin.

29
00:02:24.308 --> 00:02:27.790
In fact, it's too beautiful for a messy eater like me."

30
00:02:30.551 --> 00:02:32.952
Tom handed it back to the royal napkin holder.

31
00:02:32.972 --> 00:02:35.273
"Here, you take it.

32
00:02:35.973 --> 00:02:37.214
I'm afraid I'll get it dirty."

33
00:02:37.234 --> 00:02:40.155
"Yes, sir."

34
00:02:41.756 --> 00:02:46.898
Behind Tom's back, the royal napkin holder raised his eyebrows to the other servants.

35
00:02:48.839 --> 00:02:51.880
When Tom reached for a drink, he found that his cup was empty.

36
00:02:54.436 --> 00:02:56.417
"My apologies, Your Highness."

37
00:02:57.718 --> 00:02:59.858
Another servant was holding a pitcher of water.

38
00:03:01.919 --> 00:03:05.621
"I didn't get a chance to fill your cup before you sat down."

39
00:03:05.641 --> 00:03:08.462
"Who are you?"

40
00:03:09.002 --> 00:03:09.803
Tom asked.

41
00:03:09.823 --> 00:03:12.644
"The royal cupbearer."

42
00:03:15.045 --> 00:03:17.386
The man beamed at Tom while pouring his drink.

43
00:03:19.607 --> 00:03:21.688
Tom turned to see more servants.

44
00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:25.121
"And who are you?"

45
00:03:25.482 --> 00:03:27.223
he asked another man and a woman.

46
00:03:27.243 --> 00:03:30.066
"The royal taster."

47
00:03:31.508 --> 00:03:32.789
The man bowed low.

48
00:03:32.809 --> 00:03:38.414
"My job is to taste your food to be sure that it hasn't been poisoned."

49
00:03:39.876 --> 00:03:42.959
"Well, if it were poisoned, it wouldn't be my fault!"

50
00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:47.664
A woman in a tall white hat gave the royal taster an annoyed look.

51
00:03:49.164 --> 00:03:54.188
"I'm the head chef, Your Highness, and I only serve food of the highest quality."

52
00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:02.015
The royal taster ignored her and said to Tom, "I'm here to protect you from your enemies."

53
00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:05.738
Tom gulped.

54
00:04:05.758 --> 00:04:07.939
"I have enemies?"

55
00:04:07.959 --> 00:04:12.123
"Not many," the royal taster said.

56
00:04:12.143 --> 00:04:14.665
"You'll have more when you're king."

57
00:04:17.227 --> 00:04:18.168
Tom gulped again.

58
00:04:20.616 --> 00:04:23.278
Then he pointed to a plate of brightly colored vegetables.

59
00:04:23.298 --> 00:04:25.819
"What are these?"

60
00:04:26.279 --> 00:04:27.400
he asked the head chef.

61
00:04:29.681 --> 00:04:32.303
"Your favorite vegetables, Your Highness."

62
00:04:33.684 --> 00:04:36.725
The head chef thought it was strange that he didn't recognize them.

63
00:04:36.745 --> 00:04:43.209
"You specifically requested cucumbers and carrots for today's lunch."

64
00:04:43.229 --> 00:04:47.251
"Are these all my servants?"

65
00:04:47.731 --> 00:04:50.604
Tom asked Lord Hertford, who was standing and watching him.

66
00:04:50.624 --> 00:04:54.106
"Oh no," Lord Hertford said.

67
00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:59.207
"You have 384 more, but don't worry about them now."

68
00:05:01.588 --> 00:05:04.369
Tom turned back to his meal and dug in with his hands.

69
00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:11.751
The servants had been warned not to react to his strange behavior.

70
00:05:12.811 --> 00:05:14.872
But there was no danger that anyone would laugh.

71
00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:19.143
They all felt too sad about the changes in their beloved prince.

72
00:05:22.325 --> 00:05:24.627
Observing Tom, Lord Hertford was puzzled.

73
00:05:24.647 --> 00:05:30.551
"He walks like a prince and talks like a prince," Lord Hertford thought.

74
00:05:30.571 --> 00:05:35.375
"But it's odd that he doesn't recognize the king or any of his servants.

75
00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:41.640
He's completely forgotten how to behave—and his table manners are atrocious!"

76
00:05:43.616 --> 00:05:45.618
Lord Hertford continued watching Tom.

77
00:05:45.638 --> 00:05:51.723
"It's also strange that he remembers Latin, but not Greek or French.

78
00:05:53.324 --> 00:05:57.828
He can't be an imposter because an imposter would insist that he's the prince.

79
00:05:59.169 --> 00:06:01.791
This boy has denied that he's Prince Edward."

80
00:06:03.192 --> 00:06:08.776
Lord Hertford concluded that this must be Prince Edward, and something had gone terribly wrong with his mind.

81
00:06:10.458 --> 00:06:15.449
After Tom finished his chocolate pudding and licked the bowl, there was one dish left on the table.

82
00:06:15.469 --> 00:06:22.272
"Nuts!" Tom began filling his pockets with them.

83
00:06:26.034 --> 00:06:28.075
Lord Hertford cleared his throat and frowned.

84
00:06:28.095 --> 00:06:34.317
"That probably means I shouldn't do this," Tom thought.

85
00:06:34.337 --> 00:06:36.478
"But I don't care!

86
00:06:36.498 --> 00:06:40.020
I want to eat nuts in my room, where no one can watch me."

87
00:06:42.412 --> 00:06:44.456
Suddenly Tom's nose started to itch.

88
00:06:44.657 --> 00:06:50.788
"I'm sure there are rules against a prince scratching his own nose too," he thought.

89
00:06:50.808 --> 00:06:53.333
"What should I do?"
